===Etymology===
;to give up
:{{w|Mainland Southeast Asia linguistic area|Areal}} word possibly of {{w|Austroasiatic languages|Austroasiatic}} origin ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}); compare {{cog|lus|thlah||to release; to acquit; to quit; to give up; to leave; to neglect}}, {{cog|mkh-mnc-pro|*blah||to be released, to go free}} > {{cog|omx|blaḥ}} (> {{cog|mnw|tr=plɛ̀h|t=to escape, to be free from}}, {{m|mnw|tr=həlɛ̀h|t=to let go (of), to free (from), to send (for)}}, & {{cog|cbn|tr=phəläh}}), {{cog|okz|lā}} (> {{cog|km|ក្រឡាស់||to turn; to free oneself, break away from; to change one's mind}}), etc. (ibid.), from {{cog|mkh-pro|*lah}} > {{m|mkh-pro|*lah-s ~ *las ~ *laas||to leave}}.

:{{och-l|舍|id=2}} is perhaps its exoactive derivative with suffix *''-s''/*''-h'' (ibid.)

:Schuessler also notes this word-family's parallel to {{och-l|釋}} (whose derivative {{och-l|赦}} is related by {{zh-ref|Wang (1982)}} to {{och-l|捨}} > {{och-l|舍|id=2}}), even though the different phonetics imply different Old Chinese pronuncations; the roots *''lhaʔ'' ~ *''lhak'' ~ *''lhaiʔ'' (> {{och-l|弛|tr=*l̥ajʔ}} (B-S)) are probably variants with parallel morphological and semantic developments.

